        {
          "id": 740216579,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "That's a fair assessment. The visual distraction may not be worth the code and API changes.\n\nAs a counterpoint, `proto_tree_add_expert[_format]()` already return the expert items they create, so if there is a desire to limit dissector writers' ability to modify expert info, those functions should be changed.\n\nI'm working on a separate patch which shows large packet comments by their first line only, and shows each line as a separate entry in that comment's tree when expanded. If that patch is used without this one then the expert info is a bit of extra visual noise that could be mistaken (at a glance, anyway) as part of the comment.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6020526,
            "username": "boolean263",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "David Perry",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6020526/avatar.png?v=1789862585",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/boolean263"
